---
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/remote.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
    <title>Presentation remote</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="remote-page">
      <h1>Presentation remote</h1>
      <p>The public broker sees IP addresses, topic and timing, and can disrupt or make the session unavailable. Messages are encrypted; a compromised device or anyone with the pairing code can control the presentation. Speaker notes are not supported.</p>
      <p>Joining connects this device to a public relay. A code in the URL only fills the field; it does not connect automatically.</p>
      <form id="remote-join">
        <label for="remote-code">Pairing code</label>
        <input id="remote-code" type="text" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="97" required />
        <div class="remote-actions">
          <button id="remote-join-button" type="submit">Join</button>
          <button id="remote-leave" type="button" disabled>Disconnect</button>
        </div>
      </form>
      <p id="remote-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Not connected. No relay connection.</p>
      <p id="remote-position">No presentation state yet.</p>
      <div class="remote-actions remote-navigation">
        <button id="remote-previous" type="button" disabled>← Back</button>
        <button id="remote-next" type="button" disabled>Next →</button>
      </div>
    </main>
    <script>
      import { initializeRemotePage } from '../scripts/remote';
      initializeRemotePage();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
